Grove PATCH-26: register ZEPH and ZANO in the BasicSwap console UI

PATCH-14/16/20 registered both coins with the engine (chainparams, the
coin-client factory, prepare, run.py) and PATCH-14/20 added zephyr to the
Settings page. The console's JavaScript layer and the offers page were left
half-registered: upstream's own placeholder rows carried ZANO in
offers.html / config-manager.js / offers-pricechart.js but nowhere else, and
ZEPH appeared in none of them. Audited file by file against Wownero -- the
CryptoNote coin upstream fully wires -- on 2026-09-04:

    file                                   zano   zephyr   wownero
    ui/page_settings.py                      0       4        3
    templates/settings.html                  0       9        3
    templates/offers.html                    3       0        4
    static/js/modules/config-manager.js      1       0        1
    static/js/pages/offers-pricechart.js     1       0        1
    static/js/modules/coin-manager.js        0       0        1
    static/js/modules/cache-manager.js       0       0        1
    static/js/modules/notification-manager.js 0      0        1
    static/js/pages/amm-tables.js            0       0        2
    static/js/pages/bid-page.js              0       0        1
    static/js/modules/price-manager.js       0       0        2
    static/js/modules/api-manager.js         0       0        1

Consequences before this patch: the Settings page could not render or save
Zano's fee/daemon fields (page_settings.py's POST handler subscripts
`managedaemon_<coin>` unconditionally, so saving raised KeyError -- the same
defect PATCH-20 fixed for zephyr); `CoinManager.getCoinByAnyIdentifier`
returned nothing for either coin, so the wallet page's price fetch skipped
them, the bid page's scriptless-coin tooltips treated ZANO/ZEPH as scripted,
the AMM tables could not map their names, and the offers page had no ZEPH
entry at all.

Each of the twelve files gains its rows beside Wownero's. `Zephyr.png` and
`Zephyr-20.png` (the icons offers.html and coin-manager.js reference, by the
`coin_name()` convention `<Name>.png`) are binary and travel with the applier
as `upstream/patches/assets/`, not inside this text patch.

Rebased 2026-10-06 onto basicswap v0.19.0 (277b46b0278f1cc76199f7e847988647a1b36e38). Two things moved. (1) Upstream deleted CacheManager.getCompatiblePrices and getSymbolFromCoinId in its oracle refactor, so the cache-manager.js hunk went with them. (2) CoinManager entries now carry `priceKey` instead of coingeckoId / cryptocompareId / usesCryptoCompare / usesCoinGecko, and getPriceKey returns `coin.priceKey`. The ZANO and ZEPH entries use the new shape. With the old shape a 3-way merge kept, both coins' price key was undefined, so they shared one price slot and one of them showed the other's price. The diff below is regenerated.

